/*

You are given an array of NN integers.

You can perform the following operation at most KK times:

    Choose 22 indices ii and jj such that 1≤i<j≤N1≤i<j≤N
    Set the value of AjAj​ to AiAi​.

Find the minimum number of distinct elements that could be left in AA after performing at most KK operations.
Input Format

    The first line of input will contain a single integer TT, denoting the number of test cases.
    Each test case consists of multiple lines of input.
        The first line contains a single integer NN.
        The second line contains NN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA1​,A2​,…,AN​.

Output Format

For each test case, output on a new line the minimum number of distinct elements after at most KK operations.
Constraints

    1≤T≤1041≤T≤104
    2≤N≤2⋅1052≤N≤2⋅105
    0≤K≤N0≤K≤N
    1≤Ai≤N1≤Ai​≤N
    The sum of NN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052⋅105.

Sample 1:
Input
Output

3
4 0
1 2 3 4
4 2
1 2 3 4
3 1
1 2 2

4
2
2

Explanation:

Test Case 1 : There are no operations to perform since K=2K=2. The initial array has 44 distinct elements.

Test Case 2 : We can choose (i,j)=(1,3)(i,j)=(1,3) and then (i,j)=(2,4)(i,j)=(2,4) to get the array [1,2,1,2][1,2,1,2] which has only 22 distinct elements.


*/
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

int main() {
	// your code goes here
	int T;
    cin >> T;
    while (T--) {
        int N, K;
        cin >> N >> K;

        vector<int> A(N);
        for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) cin >> A[i];

        unordered_map<int,int> freq, first;
        for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {
            freq[A[i]]++;
            if (!first.count(A[i]))
                first[A[i]] = i;
        }
        
        int keepVal = -1, minIdx = N;
        for (auto &p : first) {
            if (p.second < minIdx) {
                minIdx = p.second;
                keepVal = p.first;
            }
        }

        vector<int> removable;
        for (auto &p : freq) {
            if (p.first != keepVal)
                removable.push_back(p.second);
        }

        sort(removable.begin(), removable.end());

        int removed = 0;
        for (int f : removable) {
            if (K >= f) {
                K -= f;
                removed++;
            } else break;
        }

        int distinct = freq.size();
        cout << distinct - removed << "\n";
    }

}
